            <ArticleTitle>Treatment of hepatitisC virus with direct-acting antivirals: Practical aspects and current situation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>29-37</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0014-2565(17)30180-7</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.rce.2017.07.006</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>HepatitisC virus infection is a significant public health problem. The introduction of direct-acting antiviral agents, whose efficacy is greater than 90% in all patient groups (including those with cirrhosis), has represented a highly relevant change compared with classical interferon-based therapies. Tolerance for these antiviral agents is significantly better, and the treatment duration is shorter. This review updates the treatment of hepatitisC virus infection with the new direct-acting antiviral agents.</AbstractText>
